.TH QUALCOMM\-CDI\-GENERATOR.PY 8 "2026\-03\-18" "qualcomm\-cdi\-generator 0.4" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
qualcomm\-cdi\-generator \- generate CDI configuration files for Qualcomm hardware
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B qualcomm\-cdi\-generator.py
.RB [ \-d
.IR destdir ]
.RB [ \-H
.IR hookfilename ]
.RB [ \-c
.IR cdifilename ]
.RB [ \-C
.IR class,... ]
.RB [ \-n ]
.RB [ \-v | \-vv ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B qualcomm\-cdi\-generator
probes the local system for Qualcomm hardware accelerators and writes
.IR "Container Device Interface" " (CDI)"
JSON specification files to
.IR /run/cdi/ .
Container runtimes that support the CDI specification can then use these
files to pass the relevant device nodes directly into containers.
.PP
In addition to the CDI JSON files, the tool writes a vendor hook script to
.IR /bin/vendorhook .
This script is referenced from the CDI files and is called by the container
runtime during the
.B createContainer
lifecycle event to set device node permissions to 0666.
.PP
For FastRPC device classes
.RB ( fastrpc\-cdsp " and " fastrpc\-adsp ),
the tool also bind\-mounts Hexagon DSP firmware trees found under
.I /usr/share
and exposes the board model string via the
.B MACHINE_NAME
environment variable and a bind\-mount at
.IR /run/device\-model .
.PP
The tool is typically invoked by the
.BR qualcomm\-cdi\-generator.service (8)
systemd oneshot service at boot time.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-destdir " " \fIdestdir\fR
Write all output files relative to
.I destdir
instead of the filesystem root.
Default:
.IR / .
.TP
.BR \-H ", " \-\-hookfilename " " \fIname\fR
Filename for the generated vendor hook script, placed inside
.IR destdir /bin/ .
Default:
.IR vendorhook .
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-cdifilename " " \fIbase\fR
Base filename for the CDI JSON output files.
The device class name is inserted before the file extension; for example,
a base of
.B qualcomm.json
produces
.IR qualcomm\-gpu.json ,
.IR qualcomm\-v4l2.json ,
etc.
Default:
.IR qualcomm.json .
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-classes " " \fIclass,...\fR
Comma\-separated list of device classes to generate.
When omitted all known classes are generated.
See
.B DEVICE CLASSES
below for the list of valid values.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Probe devices and log what would be written, but do not create or modify
any files.
.TP
.B \-v
Increase verbosity.
Specify once for
.B INFO
messages; twice
.RB ( \-vv )
for
.B DEBUG
messages.
Default log level is
.BR WARNING .
.SH DEVICE CLASSES
Each class corresponds to a family of Qualcomm hardware devices.
.TP
.B gpu
GPU render nodes, probed from
.IR /dev/dri/renderD* .
CDI entries are named
.IR renderD<index> .
.TP
.B v4l2
Video4Linux2 capture and output devices, probed from
.IR /dev/video* .
CDI entries are named
.IR video<index> .
.TP
.B dmaheap
DMA\-BUF heap devices, probed from
.IR /dev/dma_heap/*system .
CDI entries are named
.IR dmaheap\-system .
.TP
.B fastrpc\-cdsp
Qualcomm FastRPC Compute DSP nodes, probed from
.IR /dev/fastrpc\-cdsp* .
A paired
.I /dev/fastrpc\-cdsp\-secure
node, if present, is grouped with its non\-secure sibling rather than
appearing as a separate CDI entry.
.TP
.B fastrpc\-adsp
Qualcomm FastRPC Audio DSP nodes, probed from
.IR /dev/fastrpc\-adsp* .
A paired
.I /dev/fastrpc\-adsp\-secure
node, if present, is grouped with its non\-secure sibling.
.PP
Every class also receives a catch\-all
.BI name :all
CDI entry that selects every node of that class in a single reference.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /run/cdi/qualcomm\-<class>.json
CDI specification files, one per device class with detected nodes.
Created at runtime and not persistent across reboots.
.TP
.I /bin/vendorhook
Generated vendor hook script invoked by the container runtime during
container creation to set device node permissions.
.TP
.I /usr/share/*/*/*/*/dsp/
Hexagon DSP firmware directories bind\-mounted into containers for
FastRPC device classes.
.TP
.I /sys/firmware/devicetree/base/model
Read to obtain the board model string, exposed as the
.B MACHINE_NAME
container environment variable and bind\-mounted at
.IR /run/device\-model
(FastRPC classes only).
.TP
.I /lib/systemd/system/qualcomm\-cdi\-generator.service
Systemd oneshot unit that invokes this tool at boot.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR systemd.service (5)
